.TH SPRITE_FROM 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
sprite_from \- Slice a texture into frame_w x frame_h cells and return the Sprite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqsprite.h\(dq
.BI "Sprite sprite_from(Texture *tex, int frame_w, int frame_h);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Slice a texture into frame_w x frame_h cells and return the Sprite. columns is derived from the texture width, so a 128\-pixel\-wide sheet of 16\-pixel frames has 8 columns and frame 9 is row 1, column 1. Rows are implied by the height. A NULL texture yields a Sprite that draws nothing. For a single image, pass its full width and height and always draw frame 0.
.SH RETURN VALUE
the Sprite, by value.
.SH MODULE
sprite (src/engine/sprite/sprite.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sprite_draw (3),
.BR assets_texture (3),
.BR Sprite (3),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
